>> title: Sweet Potato Pie
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: sweet potato, custard, pie, dessert, southern
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: sweet potato pie, sweet potato custard pie, potato pie
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the pie comes out with the centre still moving, because one baked firm has already gone grainy by the time you see it
>> pairs-with: all-butter-pie-crust, peach-cobbler, banana-pudding

>> step: Bake the sweet potatoes rather than boiling them: boiled they carry water into the custard and it never sets.
Bake the sweet potatoes rather than boiling them.

>> step: bake whole 400°F 55 min
Bake @sweet potatoes{2%lb}(900 g) whole at 400°F (205°C) for ~bake{55%min}, until they collapse and weep at the ends.

>> step: mash with the butter
Mash @&(~1)baked sweet potatoes{} with @unsalted butter{4%Tbs}(55 g), skins pulled off.

>> step: whisk the custard smooth
Whisk @&(~1)mashed sweet potato{} with @light brown sugar{3/4%cup}(150 g), @large eggs{3}, @evaporated milk{3/4%cup}(180 mL), @ground cinnamon{1%tsp}, @ground nutmeg{1/2%tsp}, @vanilla extract{2%tsp}, @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp}.

>> step: pour into the shell, bake 350°F 45 min
Pour @&(~1)sweet potato custard{} into @pie crust{1}(9-in, blind-baked) and bake at 350°F (175°C) for ~bake{45%min}.

Cool it right down before it is cut. A warm slice slumps.
